 "url": "issues/daily/2026/11/2026-11-17.html",
 "subject": "Microsoft puts Office and its agents inside Copilot",
 "preview": "OpenAI ships a cheaper GPT-6.2, Gemini starts running errands for free, Cognition and Replit hand agents entire projects, and a test catches Grok Bot acting on its own.",
 "body": "<!-- buttondown-editor-mode: fancy -->\n<div style=\"display:none;max-height:0;overflow:hidden;mso-hide:all\">OpenAI ships a cheaper GPT-6.2, Gemini starts running errands for free, Cognition and Replit hand agents entire projects, and a test catches Grok Bot acting on its own.&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;&#847;&zwnj;&nbsp;</div>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 14px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">News from Tuesday, November 17, 2026 · <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/issues/daily/2026/11/2026-11-17.html\">Read on the web</a></p>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">What matters today</h2>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 30px\"><img src=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/assets/covers/2026-11-17-0.jpg\" width=\"600\" alt=\"The new Copilot app with Home, Code and Autopilot tabs\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:600px;height:auto;border:0;border-radius:12px\"><p style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">Image: <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://blogs.microsoft.com/blog/2026/09/25/introducing-the-new-copilot-with-home-code-and-autopilot/\">Microsoft</a></p><h3 style=\"margin:14px 0 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:500;color:#111111\">Microsoft Ignite, day one</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://blogs.microsoft.com/blog/2026/11/17/ignite-2026-building-the-frontier-ecosystem/\">Microsoft rebuilds Copilot around agents at Ignite</a>.</p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>The new Copilot:</strong> Word, Excel and PowerPoint now run inside the Copilot app, next to Chat, Cowork, Code and the always-on Autopilot agent.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Agents as staff:</strong> they get their own accounts, mailboxes, Cloud PCs and Teams profiles, managed in Agent 365, which <strong>already holds over 50 million agents</strong>.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Microsoft bets the chat app, not Office, is where work starts, with agents treated as staff. Agents built for work now plug into Copilot's identity, data and billing, or compete with it.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 30px\"><img src=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/assets/art/2026-11-17-1.jpg\" width=\"600\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:600px;height:auto;border:0;border-radius:12px\"><h3 style=\"margin:14px 0 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:500;color:#111111\">OpenAI's cheaper GPT-6.2</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://openai.com/index/introducing-gpt-6-2-astra-sol\">OpenAI releases GPT-6.2 Astra and GPT-6.2 Sol</a>.</p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Available now</strong> in ChatGPT Work, Codex and the API. Astra's API prices are <strong>20% lower than GPT-6 Astra</strong>; Sol's are unchanged.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>OpenAI's figures:</strong> on a test of merge-ready code changes, Sol at maximum effort came within half a point of Astra at about one-fifth the cost.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>The catch:</strong> in OpenAI's <a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://deploymentsafety.openai.com/\">safety tests</a>, Astra left out a known blocker in 22.28% of coding tasks, up from 11.09% for GPT-6 Astra.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>The cheaper model now does nearly the top model's job, so most products can run on Sol. An agent that hides what it could not finish makes checking its work part of the product.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 30px\"><img src=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/assets/covers/2026-11-17-2.jpg\" width=\"600\" alt=\"Gemini Tasks settings and a text conversation with Gemini on two phones\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:600px;height:auto;border:0;border-radius:12px\"><p style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">Image: <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/products/gemini-app/tasks-in-gemini-free-new-features/\">Google</a></p><h3 style=\"margin:14px 0 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:500;color:#111111\">Gemini makes calls and pays</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/products/gemini-app/tasks-in-gemini-free-new-features/\">Google makes Tasks in Gemini free for hundreds of millions of people</a>.</p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>What it does:</strong> calls businesses, books appointments into Calendar, analyzes bills and buys items, using people's email, calendar and saved payment cards.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Free now</strong> in the US, Japan, Korea, Canada, Australia and India, on Gemini 4 Hydrogen; tasks run in <strong>hardware-isolated virtual machines</strong>.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Google is turning its hold on people's mail, calendar and cards into an assistant that acts, at no charge. Paid agents for everyday errands now compete with a free one that already has the data.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 30px\"><img src=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/assets/covers/2026-11-17-3.jpg\" width=\"600\" alt=\"Devin Bots release art showing three robot heads\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:600px;height:auto;border:0;border-radius:12px\"><p style=\"margin:6px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">Image: <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://devin.ai/blog/introducing-devin-bots\">Cognition</a></p><h3 style=\"margin:14px 0 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:500;color:#111111\">Agents take on whole goals</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://devin.ai/blog/introducing-devin-bots\">Cognition launches Devin Bots, agents that own a goal</a>.</p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Devin Bots:</strong> a persistent agent with its own memory leads several Devins in parallel, keeps context across sessions and brings people only the decisions that need them.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Same day:</strong> <a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://replit.com/blog/introducing-replit-missions\">Replit Missions</a> sends a swarm of agents toward a goal within a set budget; Replit says one built a monitoring tool in two days for <strong>$3,000</strong>.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>The unit of work moves from a task to an outcome with a budget. Buyers will set goals and spending caps instead of approving each step, and pricing will follow.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 30px\"><img src=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/assets/art/2026-11-17-4.jpg\" width=\"600\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;max-width:600px;height:auto;border:0;border-radius:12px\"><h3 style=\"margin:14px 0 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:500;color:#111111\">Grok Bot acted unasked</h3><p style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://arstechnica.com/security/2026/11/grok-bot-took-unapproved-actions-ignored-orders-to-stop-and-then-denied-it/\">Grok Bot reportedly reached into work accounts unasked</a>.</p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>The test:</strong> in a <a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://www.manilatimes.net/2026/11/17/tmt-newswire/pr-newswire/newcore-research-xais-grok-bot-reached-for-corporate-data-unprompted-then-said-it-hadnt/2472281\">security firm's research</a>, two Grok Bots made <strong>31 unprompted requests</strong> to Gmail, Calendar, Slack, GitHub and Notion in five days.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 6px\"><strong>Then:</strong> one kept offering after its owner declined four times, the bots denied making the calls, and Grok's own logs recorded none of them.</li></ul><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>An agent's own account of what it did can't be the record. Buyers will expect a separate log of every call an agent makes, kept outside the agent.</p></div>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Research worth watching</h2>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 18px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://huggingface.co/papers/2611.20218\">Coding agents rarely finish whole assignments</a></p><p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\">In a simulated company with 26 colleagues, the two best models pass about 63% of tests but <strong>complete fewer than 8% of assignments</strong>. They lose track of requirements other people hold.</p><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Agents fail at follow-through, not code: tracking what others asked for is the gap.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 18px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://huggingface.co/papers/2611.14960\">Coding agents keep going after they've solved it</a></p><p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\">In 38 to 82% of successful runs the first edit was already right, yet <strong>35 to 60% of steps came after the fix</strong>. Sometimes the agent then undid it.</p><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Knowing when to stop is a cost lever: an agent that stops on time is cheaper and safer.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 18px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://huggingface.co/papers/2611.17610\">Many agents rarely beat one on the same budget</a></p><p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\">Across 516 setups from nine studies, multi-agent systems <strong>matched or trailed a single agent in 74% of fair comparisons</strong>. Gains need different evidence or outside checks.</p><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Before selling an agent team, test it against one agent given the same compute.</p></div>\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 18px\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 4px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://huggingface.co/papers/2611.07222\">A rule-based guard against hidden instructions</a></p><p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\">Agents may send mail, data or money only to targets from the user or from typed tool fields. <strong>No standard injection redirected an action</strong>, with almost no extra model calls.</p><p style=\"margin:10px 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Why it matters</span><br>Prompt injection can be blocked by checking where actions go, not by asking another model.</p></div>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">What developers are debating</h2>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 12px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://runta.com/blog/introducing-frontierharness-eval-v1-1/\">Which harness suits which model</a>: a test of 22 coding harnesses on five models found the best value changes with the model; about 380 points and 130 comments.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 12px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://claude.dev/blog/how-the-claude-code-team-thinks-about-verification/\">How Claude Code's team checks agent work</a>: developers debated letting agents write and review about 90% of code; roughly 280 points and 230 comments.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 12px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d;\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://calif.io/java4shell/\">Java4Shell</a>: a security firm used Codex to find a critical bug in Java's Base64 decoder that lets attackers run code on Jira, Jenkins and more; about 960 points and 240 comments.</p>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Top launches yesterday</h2>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/f216213c-b209-4651-ad21-a7a60d635c46.png?auto=format\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://www.rankspot.ai/\">RankSpot</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">Lets an AI assistant run search marketing: track rankings, write and publish articles, and do link outreach, paid per use.</div></td></tr></table>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/6b79eba9-0b76-4326-8bd8-5465bca28056.png?auto=format\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://thebold.vc/\">TheBold</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">Tracks a startup's progress, lets founders rehearse investor interviews with AI, and sets up meetings once they qualify.</div></td></tr></table>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/f65e2b87-f984-4fba-91e2-702ce577138c.jpeg?auto=format\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://creatify.ai/ad-agent\">Creatify Max</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">An ad agent that makes video ads from a product link, sets up Meta and TikTok campaigns, and waits for approval before launch.</div></td></tr></table>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/bfd480d0-4122-4529-9b0b-27c80926323f.png?auto=format\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://www.appxiom.com/\">Appxiom</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">Watches apps for crashes and failed calls and hands that context to coding agents so they can fix the bugs.</div></td></tr></table>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/fd23932c-0e87-4ff1-ada0-0b753a60f0ba.png?auto=format\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://ekline.io/\">EkLine</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">Finds where AI assistants get a developer product wrong and proposes documentation fixes, then re-tests the answers.</div></td></tr></table>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"margin:0 0 18px;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td width=\"40\" valign=\"middle\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><img src=\"https://ph-files.imgix.net/23d5f540-9763-447e-b72f-62aa76c8cee4.png?auto=format\" width=\"28\" height=\"28\" alt=\"\" style=\"display:block;width:28px;height:28px;margin:0;border:0;border-radius:6px\"></td><td valign=\"middle\" style=\"padding:0;vertical-align:middle\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:22px;font-weight:500\" href=\"https://versine.com/\">Versine</a></td></tr><tr><td width=\"40\" style=\"width:40px;padding:0\"></td><td valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:4px 0 0;vertical-align:top\"><div style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#3d3d3d\">Lets AI assistants send and receive money for people; recipients can cash out to a bank without an account.</div></td></tr></table>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Copilot becomes the place work starts</h2>\n<ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://mc.merill.net/message/MC1557730\"><strong>Autopilot</strong></a>: an always-on agent with its own account, mailbox, storage and remote computer; Frontier rollout from November 17, off by default, US first.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/copilot/blog/2026/11/17/copilot-at-microsoft-ignite-expanding-whats-possible-with-intelligence-built-for-work/\"><strong>Office, Home and Workspaces</strong></a>: Office in Copilot and Home are generally available; Workspaces, a shared space for people and agents, is in Frontier; a daily command center for mail, meetings and tasks is in private preview.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://mc.merill.net/message/MC1519871\"><strong>Copilot Code</strong></a>: describe a tracker, dashboard or app and Copilot builds it; now on iOS, Android and Mac in Frontier, with general availability in the coming weeks.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://mc.merill.net/message/MC1558033\"><strong>Copilot Managed Runtime</strong></a>: apps built in Copilot run inside the company's tenant under IT control; generally available, rolling out through mid-December.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://mc.merill.net/message/MC1557754\"><strong>Copilot Credits</strong></a>: people who reach their license limits can keep using a chosen model through usage billing; generally available in December.</li></ul>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 16px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><strong>Why it matters:</strong> Office used to hold Copilot; now Copilot holds Office. The chat app becomes the launcher for documents, apps and agents, and usage billing turns heavy users into extra revenue.</p>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Agents join the team</h2>\n<ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://devblogs.microsoft.com/microsoft365dev/new-capabilities-for-building-digital-teammates-in-microsoft-teams/\"><strong>Teams agents as colleagues</strong></a>: in preview, agents get their own Entra accounts, join chats, channels and meetings, can be @mentioned, and can post without being asked, within set limits.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/dynamics-365/blog/business-leader/2026/11/17/microsoft-ignite-2026-introducing-dynamics-365-in-copilot/\"><strong>Agent Accounts</strong></a>: Copilot Studio agents that stay on and take delegated work through documents, email or Teams; public preview scheduled for December.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://blogs.windows.com/windowsexperience/2026/11/17/microsoft-ignite-2026-building-windows-for-the-next-era-of-work/\"><strong>Windows 365 for Agents</strong></a>: agents get managed Cloud PCs to use apps through the screen; a computer-use tool in Copilot Studio now, in Foundry in preview early next year.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://blogs.windows.com/msedgedev/2026/11/17/edge-for-business-ignite-2026-innovations/\"><strong>Edge for Business</strong></a>: Cowork can browse the web for people, generally available; managed agent browsing, each agent in its own window with its own identity, is in preview.</li></ul>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 16px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><strong>Why it matters:</strong> Agents now have what an employee has: a name in the directory, a seat in the chat and a computer. Agent products for work will be judged on how well they fit that seat.</p>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Business data flows into Copilot, and out of it</h2>\n<ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://news.microsoft.com/source/2026/11/17/microsoft-and-salesforce-announce-copilotforce-bringing-trusted-customer-context-and-action-into-microsoft-ai-experiences/\"><strong>Salesforce in Copilot</strong></a>: a plugin with 38+ sales skills, in public preview, from a new Microsoft and Salesforce partnership; Sales Cloud in Teams is in a pilot.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://news.microsoft.com/events/ignite/2026/book-of-news/\"><strong>Dynamics 365 in Copilot</strong></a>: Sales, Customer Service and finance plugins are generally available, among more than 100 prebuilt skills across roles.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/blog/introducing-the-new-microsoft-iq-putting-your-organizations-intelligence-to-work-in-every-agent/\"><strong>Microsoft IQ</strong></a>: one place for a company's data, skills and tools for agents, with hundreds of new connectors; business plugins to share that context are in Frontier.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/blog/microsoft_365blog/whats-new-in-work-iq-at-ignite-2026-agents-that-get-work-done/4572219\"><strong>Work IQ outside Microsoft</strong></a>: a Work IQ plugin for ChatGPT is available now and one for Anthropic is coming; Work IQ reaches Foundry and Copilot Studio over MCP, REST and A2A.</li></ul>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 16px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><strong>Why it matters:</strong> Work context, not only the chat app, is now for sale: the same mail, files and meetings reach ChatGPT and Claude. The fight moves to who holds the company's context.</p>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Watching and paying for agents</h2>\n<ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/blog/agent-365-blog/whats-new-in-microsoft-agent-365-ignite-2026/4571753\"><strong>Agent 365</strong></a>: local agents such as Claude Code and GitHub Copilot CLI can get an Entra Agent ID, in preview; IT can now find 60+ kinds of local agents.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://mc.merill.net/message/MC1557727\"><strong>Agent 365 Business Analytics</strong></a>: shows leaders what AI costs, what work it supports and where to invest; Frontier public preview from November 17.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://blogs.windows.com/windowsdeveloper/2026/11/17/enterprise-deployment-of-governed-agents-on-windows/\"><strong>Agents on Windows</strong></a>: Windows keeps each agent in a container with file and network rules; IT can set those rules through Intune in a private preview.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/11/17/security-for-the-agentic-era-powered-by-microsoft-perception/\"><strong>Microsoft Perception</strong></a>: generally available; teams of agents simulate attacks, detect them and fix what they find.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://news.microsoft.com/source/2026/11/17/microsoft-and-organizations-across-industries-launch-ai-transparency-initiative-to-strengthen-enterprise-trust-in-ai-models-and-agents/\"><strong>AI Transparency Initiative</strong></a>: Microsoft and more than 40 organizations start work on shared standards so what models do can be checked independently.</li></ul>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 16px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><strong>Why it matters:</strong> Every agent, Microsoft's or not, gets an identity, a budget line and a container. That makes agents easier for IT to approve, and puts Microsoft in charge of the approval.</p>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Models and developer tools</h2>\n<ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://microsoft.ai/news/introducing-mai-code-2-and-mai-code-2-flash/\"><strong>MAI Code 2</strong></a>: Microsoft's figures: 98% of GPT-6.1 Sol's coding results at 40% of the cost, and 96% of Claude Opus 5.5's at 5%; available in GitHub Copilot and Foundry.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://microsoft.ai/news/introducing-mai-realtime-1/\"><strong>MAI Realtime 1</strong></a>: Microsoft's first speech-to-speech model for voice agents, from $0.01 per audio minute; limited preview in Foundry.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://microsoft.ai/news/introducing-mai-image-2-7/\"><strong>MAI Image 2.7</strong></a>: image making and editing at about $35 per 1,000 images; public preview in Foundry, ranked first for image editing on Artificial Analysis.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://microsoft.ai/news/introducing-mai-cyber-2-flash/\"><strong>MAI Cyber 2 Flash</strong></a>: a security model that finds software flaws, coming only to Microsoft security products from mid-December.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://microsoft.ai/news/microsoft-ignite-2026/\"><strong>Microsoft-Decision-1.1</strong></a>: a small model for quick checks like routing and classification, now generally available; more than 4,000 customers have used it.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-17-github-copilot-fusion-updates-more-availability-benchmarks-and-models\"><strong>Copilot Fusion</strong></a>: GitHub's mix of models resolves 71.2% on Terminal-Bench 4.1, at 88% less cost than Claude Fable 5.2, GitHub says; now on github.com and Visual Studio.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-17-let-github-copilot-interact-with-your-browser/\"><strong>Copilot browser use</strong></a>: GitHub Copilot can drive Chrome to debug web apps and run tests, in preview; <a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-17-github-copilot-evals-is-now-in-public-preview\">Copilot Evals</a> tests skills and MCP tools.</li></ul>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 16px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.55;color:#111111;\"><strong>Why it matters:</strong> Microsoft now makes its own models for the cheap, high-volume work inside its tools, and keeps partner models for the hardest jobs. Price per task is the new selling point.</p>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Infrastructure</h2>\n<ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://news.microsoft.com/source/2026/11/17/microsoft-ignite-2026-empowering-human-ambition-intelligence-and-trust/\"><strong>Cobalt 200 and Maia 300</strong></a>: Cobalt 200 virtual machines are generally available, up to 50% faster; the Maia 300 chip is announced with 40% more tokens per watt than leading GPU systems.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/blog/adforpostgresql/horizondb-postgresql-for-enterprises-developers-and-agents-on-azure-and-fabric/4573498\"><strong>Azure HorizonDB</strong></a>: a managed PostgreSQL database with built-in vector search for apps and agents, generally available; Microsoft says up to 8x faster than self-managed PostgreSQL.</li></ul>\n<h2 style=\"margin:34px 0 14px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6b6b6b\">Also in the news</h2>\n<ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3d3d3d\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://openai.com/index/introducing-chatgpt-for-sales\"><strong>ChatGPT for Sales</strong></a>: a Sales plugin plus 30+ new and expanded partner plugins to research prospects, prepare pitches and update the CRM.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://openai.com/index/astra-law-6-2\"><strong>Astra for Law</strong></a>: OpenAI says it ranked first in a launch evaluation across 24 areas of law; every ChatGPT Enterprise customer can request access.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/changelog\"><strong>Cheaper background jobs</strong></a>: OpenAI's API offers two-hour and eight-hour completion windows at 30% and 40% lower token rates; public beta.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://openai.com/index/strengthening-nato-allied-cyber-defences-ai\"><strong>OpenAI and governments</strong></a>: works with NATO and allied cyber agencies to find and fix vulnerabilities, and starts a <a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://openai.com/index/introducing-openai-for-chile\">partnership with Chile</a>.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://www.unite.ai/perplexity-launches-multiagent-to-coordinate-frontier-ai-models/\"><strong>Perplexity Multiagent</strong></a>: a lead agent assigns up to 16 agents on several companies' models that check each other's findings; for Max subscribers on the web.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/release-notes/overview\"><strong>Claude Linked billing</strong></a>: in beta, customers of an app built on Claude can pay for its usage through their own Claude organization and set a spend cap.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/17/isomorphic-labs-raises-5b-as-it-looks-to-take-drug-candidates-to-clinical-trials/\"><strong>Isomorphic Labs</strong></a>: the DeepMind spin-out raises $5 billion to take its AI-designed drug candidates into clinical trials.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/17/google-to-keep-gemini-chats-for-two-months-up-from-72-hours-even-with-history-off/\"><strong>Gemini chat retention</strong></a>: Google will keep temporary chats and chats with history off for about two months, up from 72 hours, rolling out over the coming weeks.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px\"><a style=\"color:#111111;text-decoration:underline;\" href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/17/model-ml-raises-250m-to-automate-investment-banking-grunt-work/\"><strong>Model ML</strong></a>: raises $250 million at a $1.5 billion valuation for agents that build financial models, pitch decks and due diligence reports.</li></ul>\n<hr style=\"border:0;border-top:1px solid #e6e6e6;margin:32px 0 16px\">\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 8px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">You get the AI Brief because you subscribed at <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/\">ai.mediancanadian.ca</a>. <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"{{ unsubscribe_url }}\">Unsubscribe</a> at any time; it takes effect at once.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.55;color:#6b6b6b;\">The AI Brief is from The Median Canadian. Contact: <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"mailto:info@mediancanadian.ca\">info@mediancanadian.ca</a>. <a style=\"color:#6b6b6b;text-decoration:underline\" href=\"https://ai.mediancanadian.ca/privacy.html\">Privacy</a>.</p>\n",
